<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Japan</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Japanese</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Japan is an island nation in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-asia">East Asia</a>. It absorbed many influences from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty">Tang Dynasty</a> and resisted the invasions of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuan-dynasty">Yuan Dynasty</a>, was unified under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokugawa-shogunate">Tokugawa Shogunate</a>, and traded with Portuguese and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> merchants. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meiji-restoration">Meiji Restoration</a> it became the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/empire-of-japan">Empire of Japan</a>, which defeated the Qing and Russian empires and attacked British and Dutch possessions in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia">Asia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/japan.jpg" alt="Japan" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Various · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Japan.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Argentina remained neutral in both world wars until it declared war on Germany and <b>Japan</b> in March 1945.</blockquote><a href="/empire/argentine-republic">Argentine Republic · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>Deerskins went in quantity to <b>Japan</b>, while regular tribute missions to the Ming and later the Qing courts doubled as trading voyages.</blockquote><a href="/empire/ayutthaya-kingdom">Ayutthaya Kingdom · Socioeconomy</a></li><li><blockquote>Sea routes linked Baekje with the southern Chinese courts, the Gaya states and the Japanese archipelago, bringing silks, ceramics and books from China and carrying Baekje goods, scholars and artisans to <b>Japan</b>.</blockquote><a href="/empire/baekje">Baekje · Socioeconomy</a></li><li><blockquote>The Tang Xuanming calendar, which <b>Japan</b> used for more than 800 years from 862, first reached Japan with an embassy from Balhae.</blockquote><a href="/empire/balhae">Balhae · At a glance</a></li><li><blockquote>…in August 1945, and the Anglo-American loan negotiated to replace it was not finally repaid until 2006, while <b>Japan</b>'s rapid conquest of Hong Kong, Malaya, Singapore and Burma in 1941–1942 — the fall of Singapore in February 1942 above all — shattered the myth of British invincibility in…</blockquote><a href="/empire/british-empire">British Empire · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>In the Second World War the Indian Army grew to about 2.5 million men, often called the largest volunteer army in history, and helped defeat <b>Japan</b> in Burma after the battles of Imphal and Kohima in 1944.</blockquote><a href="/empire/british-raj">British Raj · Military</a></li></ul></section>
